      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "Before we get started, I want to build a proof of concept to understand that the business workflow can be automated safely and usefully. \n\nI have a lot of choices in where I build. But I want to use the GitHub Copilot app, the only desktop experience for agent-driven development built natively on GitHub. This gives me one command center for everything I have in flight — active work, open issues, pending reviews, the automations I've set up. This is where I start every morning. And if I want to go deeper, any session hands straight into VS Code — no juggling CLIs or SDKs. ",
      "demo_actions": "Open the GitHub Copilot app. Briefly orient the viewer to the home screen and top-level navigation. Pause long enough to call out active work, issues, reviews, and automations.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_111553_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.15.31@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
