        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "Let me prove Caldova's idea. One prompt — “start the contract reconciliation proof of concept” — and the app handles the setup. \n\nFirst, it spins up an isolated worktree: my own workspace to experiment freely, with nothing touching the main branch or anyone else's work. ",
      "demo_actions": "Move into the working area and enter the prompt to start the proof of concept. Show the setup beginning and briefly point out that a new worktree is being created.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_111801_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.17.40@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "Then it loads a custom skill I built for this exact reconciliation workflow. That carries the domain knowledge and the steps, so every session starts with Caldova's context instead of me rebuilding it. \n\nAnd before anything runs, it checks the local model with a quick preflight. ",
      "demo_actions": "Show the skill loading and the preflight check. Call out the custom skill for the scenario and the Ollama validation step.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112228_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.18.47@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "Here's the app. On the left, the Copilot session driving the work. On the right, the Canvas — a live, interactive view of the app I'm building. \n\nThis is the part to watch. I'm not just chatting with an agent. I can click inside the Canvas, trigger a step, and the Canvas talks back to the agent. Think of it as a modern, shareable version of local-host development — something I can check into a repo or hand to a teammate. \n\nRight now I'm on my local model, and I can switch to cloud at any time. ",
      "demo_actions": "Open the Canvas and orient the viewer to the layout. Point out the Copilot session on the left, the interactive Canvas on the right, and the current model selection.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112324_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.20.38@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
